From cff7ed8862e5474c71db71f93b346ac691f55a10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hiper25 <whydonit@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 02:51:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] tee: optee: use negotiated reserved command pool for SC2

The matched firmware rejects command pages in part of normal-world RAM.
Prefer its negotiated reserved pool without disabling external dynamic
SHM registration or changing generic firmware allocation.

Change-Id: I2eecd385fe86168f11cf96e96cd71c246d74ae80
---
 .../bindings/arm/firmware/linaro,optee-tz.yaml           | 5 +++++
 drivers/tee/optee/smc_abi.c                              | 9 ++++++++-
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/firmware/linaro,optee-tz.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/firmware/linaro,optee-tz.yaml
index e3a97ac70e6675b3c965c7408e01223f9b92f917..b090e7f0631308ea8cce6662472ad46025cb7a35 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/firmware/linaro,optee-tz.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/firmware/linaro,optee-tz.yaml
@@ -24,6 +24,11 @@ description: |
   clients must not issue GET_THREAD_COUNT and must use the existing
   unknown-thread-count operation instead.
 
+  This firmware rejects command buffers in some otherwise usable
+  normal-world RAM. Driver allocations must use the reserved shared-memory
+  pool returned by GET_SHM_CONFIG. This does not override the advertised
+  dynamic shared-memory capability for external buffer registration.
+
 properties:
   $nodename:
     const: optee
diff --git a/drivers/tee/optee/smc_abi.c b/drivers/tee/optee/smc_abi.c
index b16356059e63950a934f1ea266e3940fab43eb11..c789d0b37469e1c6373e24dca6a9812988b3ed7e 100644
--- a/drivers/tee/optee/smc_abi.c
+++ b/drivers/tee/optee/smc_abi.c
@@ -1768,7 +1768,14 @@ static int optee_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	/*
 	 * Try to use dynamic shared memory if possible
 	 */
-	if (sec_caps & OPTEE_SMC_SEC_CAP_DYNAMIC_SHM) {
+	/*
+	 * SC2 firmware rejects argument pages in part of normal-world RAM.
+	 * Use its negotiated reserved pool for driver allocations, including
+	 * registration commands. Keep DYNAMIC_SHM for external registrations.
+	 */
+	if ((sec_caps & OPTEE_SMC_SEC_CAP_DYNAMIC_SHM) &&
+	    !of_device_is_compatible(pdev->dev.of_node,
+				     "amlogic,meson-sc2-optee-tz")) {
 		/*
 		 * If we have OPTEE_SMC_SEC_CAP_RPC_ARG we can ask
 		 * optee_get_msg_arg() to pre-register (by having
